{# IntelEngine tales: which of a story step's prepared outcomes a conversation turned into (TaleAuthor.cpp SendJudge).
   Context: npc_name, player_name, goal (the step), transcript (the conversation's lines, oldest first), outcomes (key
   o0..o2, text), allow_none (false once two readings found nothing: the closest outcome must be named). The keys o0,
   o1, o2 and "none" are the contract with TaleAuthor.cpp. Without a decision provider the chat form answers
   (intel_tale_turn_chat.prompt). #}
[ state conversation ]
{% if decision %}{{ player_name }} has a decision to make in front of {{ npc_name }}: {{ goal }}
{% else %}{{ player_name }} has been talking with {{ npc_name }}. What {{ player_name }} set out to do: {{ goal }}
{% endif %}
{{ transcript }}
[ end state ]

[ question turn choice ]
{% if decision %}
Read the conversation above. Has {{ player_name }} already told {{ npc_name }} their decision, in their own words? Name the answer that says the same as what {{ player_name }} actually said to {{ npc_name }}. Only {{ player_name }}'s own lines count, and only a plain statement of it: a question, a hint, a greeting, or words about something else is no decision, and then the answer is none.
{% else %}
Read the conversation above. Which of these outcomes has it come to, going only by what was actually said? An outcome about {{ npc_name }} has happened only when {{ npc_name }}'s own lines say it: what {{ player_name }} claims, asks or already knows is not {{ npc_name }}'s answer, and neither is a greeting, a gesture or talk about something else.
{% if allow_none %}
If none of them has happened yet, answer none.
{% else %}
Name the outcome closest to where the conversation ended.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
[ criteria ]
{% for o in outcomes %}
{{ o.key }}: {{ o.text }}
{% endfor %}
{% if allow_none %}
{% if decision %}none: {{ player_name }} has not plainly told {{ npc_name }} any of these yet.
{% else %}none: None of these has happened yet; the conversation has not come to it.
{% endif %}{% endif %}
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
